    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1050">

                <pb facs="0880" n="870" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg870"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 Bacon, Leonard Lee: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kohler</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-04-23T14:00:00+03:00">April 23, 1949—2
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 23—9:21 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1020. Still unable elicit answer Bacon visa, reDeptel 244, 21st.<anchor n="24"
                        xml:id="d1050-f1"/> Not informed of date Colling application but have sent
                    note Foreign Office. Doubtful Colling visa can be obtained prior next sailing
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Smolny</hi>, exact date of which unknown here, but
                    will continue press.</p>
                <p>Repeated Shanghai 9, Dairen 22, Nanking 46.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kohler</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1050-f1" n="24" xml:id="d1050-f1-content">
                <p>Same as telegram No. 709 to Shanghai, <ref target="#pg867">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">ibid</hi>
                    </ref>.</p>
            </note>
